{"content": "RAINBOW 3D — COMPLETE ACCOUNT RECOVERY & CONTINUATION\n\nClaude, I am switching to this Claude account because my previous account ran out of credits.\n\nTHIS IS MY EXISTING RAINBOW 3D GAME. DO NOT RESTART, REDESIGN, OR REBUILD IT FROM SCRATCH.\n\nMy GitHub repository:\nhttps://github.com/josiahscalia5-dev/rainbow-\n\nMy source branch:\n\"ccr-937c7fbb-htsrgt\"\n\n1. RECOVER MY ENTIRE PROJECT\n\nConnect to my private GitHub repository and fetch the latest commits.\n\nImportant: Other Claude sessions have also worked on this project. Check the latest recovery, account-transfer and working branches so no newer work is accidentally missed.\n\nRead these existing handoff documents:\n\n- \"backups/CLAUDE_ACCOUNT_TRANSFER.md\"\n- \"backups/START_NEW_CLAUDE_ACCOUNT.md\"\n- \"CLAUDE.md\"\n\nRun the project's saved recovery script if available.\n\nCreate a NEW safe working branch from the most complete verified project state.\n\nNever force-push, overwrite, delete or reset my original branches.\n\nRestore all eleven gameplay screens, characters, 3D models, animations, textures, code, approved reference images, screenshots, Blender projects, QA tests and Android files.\n\nVerify all Git LFS assets are real files, not pointers.\n\n2. RESTORE ALL TEN SPECIALIST AGENTS\n\nLoad all ten original specialists from \".claude/agents/\".\n\nPreserve their exact instructions, specialized skills, tools, progress reports and unfinished tasks.\n\nMy previous session had FOUR specialists working on Screen 05:\n\n1. path-camera-transition-engineer\n\n- Correct the distant winding S-curve.\n- Continue the gold coin trail into the golden light.\n- Fix distant ring spacing and tunnel depth.\n- Keep the approved camera and game transitions intact.\n\n2. washer-environment-modeler\n\n- Improve the glowing metallic gold rings.\n- Match the glossy magenta-purple washer walls.\n- Fix the rounded gold washer fittings.\n- Improve the distant golden lighting.\n- Incorporate useful Marble World Labs reflections and wall textures.\n\n3. water-fx-specialist\n\n- Recreate the thick, vibrant electric-blue water.\n- Add broad, flowing pink S-shaped bands.\n- Improve glossy reflections, sparkle, flowing waves and water depth.\n\n4. foam-bubbles-particles\n\n- Replace large white foam heaps with fine continuous bubble banks.\n- Create natural water splashes behind Benny.\n- Improve the transparent floating soap bubbles.\n\nRead their latest saved work and relaunch unfinished specialists. Do not duplicate completed work.\n\nKeep their file responsibilities separate so they cannot overwrite one another.\n\n3. RESTORE MARBLE WORLD LABS — VERY IMPORTANT\n\nWe already generated TWO Marble World Labs 3D worlds using my approved Screen 05 artwork.\n\nDO NOT LOSE THEM OR GENERATE THEM AGAIN UNNECESSARILY.\n\nRecover from GitHub:\n\n- Both Marble-generated worlds.\n- Their world IDs and generation metadata.\n- All available 3D splat sizes.\n- \".ply\" files.\n- Collision meshes and GLB files.\n- Panorama images.\n- Marble wall textures.\n- Blender import projects.\n- Generated thumbnails.\n- Camera alignment and reconstruction scripts.\n- Original generation prompts.\n- World Labs credit ledger and asset manifests.\n\nInspect the saved World Labs project folders, including \"qa/worldlabs/05/\".\n\nMy last reported World Labs API balance was approximately 5,190 credits. Verify the current balance using a free authorized check if credentials are connected.\n\nMy World Labs account is separate from my Claude account.\n\nHelp me reconnect the existing World Labs Developer API using a SECURE credential form. Never ask me to paste my API key into ordinary chat or store it in GitHub.\n\nRestore the official World Labs plugin and Atlas connector where available, but remember Atlas and Marble are separate services.\n\nUSE THE EXISTING MARBLE ASSETS IN MY REAL GAME.\n\nSpecifically:\n\n- Use the full-quality Marble panorama for Screen 05 reflection lighting when it produces a closer match.\n- Use the Marble wall textures to improve the glossy metallic purple tunnel.\n- Use Marble's 3D measurements and geometry to guide ring positions, walls and fittings.\n- Use Blender to rebuild or optimize any useful geometry for Android.\n\nDo not substitute a static Marble image or heavy splat scene for my real playable game.\n\nNo additional paid generations or mesh exports without my approval.\n\n4. CONTINUE MY APPROVED SCREEN 05\n\nTHIS IS MY NUMBER ONE DESIGN PRIORITY.\n\nMy original approved image is called:\n\n05 · FLOW INTO THE CURRENT\n\nI want my REAL playable Android game to look approximately 90–95% like my original approved screenshot, if achievable.\n\nPreserve Benny's pink fluffy body, purple-and-white striped beanie, purple pom-pom and yellow star.\n\nMatch these visual features:\n\n1. Deep, glossy, metallic purple washing-machine tunnel.\n2. Perfectly proportioned reflective gold rings.\n3. Correctly shaped rounded gold wall fittings.\n4. Thick, highly polished cyan-and-pink water.\n5. Dramatic winding S-curves leading into the distant golden light.\n6. Accurate gold dollar-token placement.\n7. Small iridescent soap bubbles.\n8. Fine foam banks and realistic splash effects.\n9. Premium lighting, reflections and depth.\n10. Exact approved behind-the-character camera composition.\n\nPreserve the previously locked Screen 05 camera and corrected river geometry unless a carefully tested change is required.\n\nPrioritize substantial visual improvements over endless tiny adjustments.\n\nMy approved screenshot ALWAYS takes priority over the Marble-generated artwork.\n\n5. RESTORE ALL DEVELOPMENT TOOLS AND SERVERS\n\nVerify and restore the existing project toolchain:\n\n- Blender 5.3 or compatible version.\n- Three.js and WebGL.\n- Playwright MCP and screenshot testing.\n- GitHub connection.\n- Android SDK and build tools.\n- Capacitor.\n- World Labs plugin.\n- Marble World API integration.\n- Atlas connector when available.\n- All existing MCP