w a session's last turn ended, call list_events with kinds [\"result\"] and limit 100.", "name": "mcp__claude-code-remote__list_sessions", "schema": {"description": "List Claude Code Remote sessions visible to the authenticated account. In bot contexts (e.g. Slack) this is a shared pool spanning many people, not just the human asking — pass mine: true to narrow to sessions started by the same account as the calling session. Returns session IDs, titles, statuses, and timestamps. status_bucket is the board bucket (working / blocked / review_ready / completed / failed) — read this for \"running / waiting on you / done / errored\"; updated_at is the last event. Where shown, a row also has parent_session_id, task_summary and post_turn_summary (recent_action, needs_action). To read how a session's last turn ended, call list_events with kinds [\"result\"] and limit 100.", "eager_input_streaming": true, "input_schema": {"properties": {"after_id": {"description": "Pagination cursor: return sessions older than this session ID. Pass the last_id from a previous response to get the next page.", "type": "string"}, "before_id": {"description": "Pagination cursor: return sessions newer than this session ID. Pass the first_id from a previous response to get the previous page.", "type": "string"}, "children": {"description": "Set true to narrow the list to the sessions that this session created with create_session. Their rows add post_turn_summary.status_category, that session's post-turn classifier verdict (omitted when none), and connection_status=\"disconnected\", which means that session's worker died mid-turn and it is doing no work. A page can hold fewer rows than limit (even none) while has_more is true — keep passing last_id as after_id. Not with tags.", "type": "boolean"}, "limit": {"description": "Maximum number of sessions to return (default 20, max 100).", "type": "integer"}, "mine": {"description": "Filter to sessions started by the same account as the calling session. U